    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (17 tests, BUILD SUCCESS) \u2014 the acceptance suite (Cp01\u2013Cp09 plus base helpers) is the only test set in the repo, and all of it passes including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented server-assigned `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` on owner creation.\n\n**What the format means (per spec & test):** LAST3 = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`; NNNN = 4-digit zero-padded global sequence equal to *one more than the current number of owners*. Computed before the new owner is saved, so two successive creates get consecutive numbers (`SMI-000N`, then `JON-000N+1`), which is exactly what `Cp09Tests.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` asserts.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `customerCode` field (`@Column(name=\"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` (new) \u2014 reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, counts owners via `OwnerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, and sets `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence)`. Guards short surnames with `Math.min(3, length)`.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance (so the count sees the seed data plus prior commits, but not the not-yet-saved current owner).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`; MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so the value flows out on `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n- DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column; and the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql` got a trailing `NULL` to match the new column count (h2/postgres use named-column inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nTests use the `hsqldb` profile; the initial `row column count mismatch` was the positional seed inserts, now fixed.",
